From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:01:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] urlmon/tests: the dot segment test has one field too many
 here.

Upstream's uri_parse_test has an insufficient_buffer_ok before
property2, and the "%2E." test ported with the remove_dot_segments fix
sets it.  This tree's struct has no such field, so the TRUE landed in
property2 as a pointer to address 1, read only if the result ever
failed to match.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3f3b9c42b376879e00e31a050c6f49f6ef7b6d77)

diff --git a/dlls/urlmon/tests/uri.c b/dlls/urlmon/tests/uri.c
index 405b6d8f49d..7d939ef5dee 100644
--- a/dlls/urlmon/tests/uri.c
+++ b/dlls/urlmon/tests/uri.c
@@ -8297,7 +8297,7 @@ static const uri_parse_test uri_parse_tests[] = {
     {"http://google.com/test/../",Uri_CREATE_NO_CANONICALIZE,PARSE_CANONICALIZE,URL_NO_META,"http://google.com/test/../",S_OK,FALSE},
     {"http://google.com/test/../",Uri_CREATE_NO_CANONICALIZE,PARSE_CANONICALIZE,0,"http://google.com/",S_OK,FALSE},
     {"zip://google.com/test/../",Uri_CREATE_NO_CANONICALIZE,PARSE_CANONICALIZE,0,"zip://google.com/",S_OK,FALSE},
-    {"zip://google.com/test/%2E./",Uri_CREATE_NO_CANONICALIZE,PARSE_CANONICALIZE,URL_UNESCAPE,"zip://google.com/test/../",S_OK,FALSE,TRUE},
+    {"zip://google.com/test/%2E./",Uri_CREATE_NO_CANONICALIZE,PARSE_CANONICALIZE,URL_UNESCAPE,"zip://google.com/test/../",S_OK,FALSE},
     {"file:///c:/test/../test",Uri_CREATE_NO_CANONICALIZE,PARSE_CANONICALIZE,URL_DONT_SIMPLIFY,"file:///c:/test/../test",S_OK,FALSE},
 
     /* PARSE_FRIENDLY tests. */
